course: dictionary
lesson: 13600
title: Incorporated: included or made official
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. «Incorporated» has three meanings: included as part of something bigger, officially set up as a legal business, or given its own official local government.
explain: «Her good ideas were incorporated into the class plan.» Here the clue is «into the plan»: the ideas became part of something bigger. Ask yourself what word would fit. «Included» fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «Apple Inc.» is a company name. The «Inc.» stands for incorporated, which means the company has been officially set up as a legal business. In the UK, companies use «Ltd» or «plc» instead.
explain: In cooking, «incorporate the eggs» means mix them in well. The same idea shows up again: one thing is added inside another until they become one.
fact: Incorporated means included as part of something bigger.
fact: «Inc.» after a company name stands for incorporated.
fact: An incorporated company has been officially set up as a corporation, a legal business.
fact: An incorporated town or city has its own official local government.
fact: In the UK, «Ltd» or «plc» are used instead of Inc.
exercise: «Her ideas were well incorporated into her essay.» What does incorporated mean here? | Read out loud | *Included as part of something bigger | Thrown away | Written in pencil
exercise: «Apple Inc.» is the name of a company. What does Inc. stand for? | Invented | Included | Income | *Incorporated
exercise: «Incorporate the eggs into the flour.» What should you do with the eggs? | Count them | Throw them away | Cook them alone | *Mix them in well
test: «The town became incorporated in 1890, so it now has its own council.» What does incorporated mean here? | Hidden from view | Covered in snow | *Set up with its own official local government
test: In the UK, which short form is used instead of Inc. after a company name? | Mrs | *plc | Dr | Ave
exam: «The club incorporated every idea from the class into one plan.» Which meaning fits best? | Left out every idea | Painted every idea | *Included every idea as part of the plan | Read every idea twice
